---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **「what to watch after <작품>」에 답하는 자리.** (`/what-to-watch-after`)
 *
 * ── 왜 (2026-08-30) ───────────────────────────────────────────
 * 자동완성으로 재 보니 손님이 실제로 치는 말이 이랬다 —
 *   `what to watch after squid game`  자동완성 1번째 · 그 말로 시작하는 줄 6
 *   `korean shows like squid game`    자동완성 1번째 · 4줄
 * 우리 지면 101장 가운데 **그 물음 «모양»에 답하는 것이 없었다.**
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 «절대» 하지 않는 것 ──────────────────────────
 * 이 자리는 추천으로 미끄러지기 가장 쉬운 자리다. 회사 강령이 여기서 갈린다 —
 *   「⛔ 『이렇게 하세요』는 조언이다 · ✅ 『N명 중 M명이 그렇게 했다』는 사실이다」
 *   「**우리가 바늘을 세우지 않는다.** 지형을 그려 놓고, 바늘은 보는 사람이 세운다」
 *
 * ⛔ 그래서 「비슷한 작품」·「추천작」·「이걸 보세요」를 안 쓴다. 닮음을 «재지 않는다».
 * ✅ 세는 것은 하나다 — **그 작품이 그 나라 그 주에 톱10 에 있을 때 «같은 목록에» 있던 한국 작품.**
 *   16,408 개 나라-주 칸에서 셌다. 취향이 아니라 **같은 칸에 있었던 횟수**다.
 *
 * ⚠ 뜻하는 것과 «안» 뜻하는 것을 화면에 같이 적는다 — 안 적으면 손님이 추천으로 읽는다.
 * ⛔ 화면에 한국어를 내지 않는다 — 이 주석은 frontmatter 라 나가지 않는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwMethodLimits from '../../components/KcwMethodLimits.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import data from '../../data/kcw-alongside.json';

/* 손님이 실제로 묻는 작품이 앞에 오게 — 함께 있은 나라-주 합이 큰 순서다 */
const 앞줄 = data.작품.slice(0, 24);
const 첫째 = data.작품[0];
const 칸수 = data.한국작품이든칸.toLocaleString('en-US');

const TITLE = 'What to watch after Squid Game — what was on the same Netflix top 10, in the same week';
const DESC = 'Not a recommendation list. We counted, across '
  + `${칸수} country-weeks of Netflix top 10 data, which other Korean titles were on the same `
  + `country's list in the same week. After ${첫째.title}, the title that shared the most `
  + `country-weeks was ${첫째.함께[0].제목} (${첫째.함께[0].나라주}). `
  + `${data.낸작품} Korean titles, each with the titles it sat beside.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: 앞줄.slice(0, 10).map((t: any) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: `What was on Netflix alongside ${t.title}?`,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: `In the weeks ${t.title} was in a country's Netflix top 10, the Korean title that `
        + `appeared on that same list most often was ${t.함께[0].제목}, sharing `
        + `${t.함께[0].나라주} country-weeks with it. This counts co-appearance on the same `
        + 'published list. It does not mean the same people watched both, and it is not a '
        + 'recommendation.',
    },
  })),
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/what-to-watch-after">
  <h1>What to watch after a Korean show</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    <b>We are not going to recommend anything.</b> We have no idea what you like, and any site
    that tells you otherwise is guessing at it. What we have instead is a record of what was
    actually sitting next to each title on the list you saw it on.
  </p>

  <p class="lead">
    Netflix publishes a weekly top 10 for each country. We took
    {' '}<b>{칸수} country-weeks</b> of it and counted, for every Korean title, which
    <em>other</em> Korean titles were on that same country&rsquo;s list in that same week.
    So: after <b>{첫째.title}</b>, the title that shared the most lists with it was
    {' '}<b>{첫째.함께[0].제목}</b> &mdash; the two were on the same country&rsquo;s top 10 in the
    same week <b>{첫째.함께[0].나라주} times</b>. That is a fact about a published list, and it is
    the whole of what we are claiming.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>What this number means, and what it does not.</b>
    {' '}It means two titles appeared on one country&rsquo;s published top 10 in the same week.
    {' '}<b>It does not mean the same people watched both.</b> It does not mean the two are
    similar &mdash; a horror series and a family romance can share a list all year. And it is not
    a ranking of what you should watch next. If a title sat beside another one often, that is
    mostly a fact about <em>when they were released</em> and <em>how long each stayed</em>, not
    about what they have in common.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>Big numbers here mostly mean the title lasted.</b> A show that held a country&rsquo;s top
    10 for a year will sit beside almost everything; a show that charted for one week in one
    country can sit beside at most nine other titles ever. So read the count next to the name,
    and read the &ldquo;countries&rdquo; and &ldquo;weeks&rdquo; columns with it. A small number
    is not a worse title. It is a shorter run.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The {앞줄.length} titles that shared the most lists</h2>
    <p class="fine">
      Ordered by the total number of country-weeks the title spent beside any other Korean title.
      Each row shows the three it sat beside most often. Follow a title for its own full list.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Title</th>
          <th class="num">Countries</th>
          <th class="num">Weeks</th>
          <th>Sat beside most often</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {앞줄.map((t: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="nm"><a href={`/title/${t.slug}`}><b>{t.title}</b></a></td>
            <td class="num">{t.markets}</td>
            <td class="num">{t.weeks}</td>
            <td class="fine">
              {t.함께.slice(0, 3).map((o: any, i: number) => (
                <>
                  {i > 0 && ' · '}
                  <a href={`/title/${o.slug}`}>{o.제목}</a>
                  {' '}<span class="num">({o.나라주})</span>
                </>
              ))}
            </td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="fine">
      The number in brackets is <b>country-weeks shared</b> &mdash; how many times the two were on
      one country&rsquo;s Netflix top 10 in the same week.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Every title we could do this for</h2>
    <p>
      <b>{data.낸작품} Korean titles</b> out of the {data.지면있는작품} we hold a page for had at
      least one other Korean title share a list with them. The rest charted alone every week they
      charted &mdash; in those countries, in those weeks, theirs was the only Korean title on the
      list. That is worth knowing too, and it is why we do not quietly drop them: a title with no
      neighbours is not a title that failed.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      We only link to titles that have a page here, so a title&rsquo;s real list of neighbours can
      be longer than what we show. Where we cut it, we cut at twelve.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwShorts set="alongside-voiced" says={`Fourteen seconds, read aloud: ${첫째.title} and ${첫째.함께[0].제목} were on the same country's Netflix top 10, in the same week, ${첫째.함께[0].나라주} times — and even that closest pair is only a tenth of all the country-weeks ${첫째.title} shared with anything. This counts one published list. It is not a count of people, and Netflix releases no viewer data at all.`} />

  <KcwMethodLimits
    method={{
      Source: `Netflix Tudum weekly country top 10, file ${data.원자료}`,
      Rows: `${data.읽은줄.toLocaleString('en-US')} read, ${data.못읽은줄} unreadable`,
      Counted: 'Country-weeks in which two Korean titles were both in that country\'s top 10',
      Scope: `${data.한국작품이든칸.toLocaleString('en-US')} country-weeks contained at least one Korean title`,
      Measured: data.잰날.slice(0, 10),
    }}
    limitation={{
      'Not a recommendation': 'Co-appearance on a list is not similarity, and not a suggestion.',
      'Not shared viewers': 'Netflix publishes no per-viewer data. We cannot tell who watched what.',
      'Length dominates': 'Longer runs produce larger counts almost mechanically.',
      'Korean titles only': 'We count a title as Korean only if it is in our own table of 974. Titles we do not hold are invisible here, even if they were on the same list.',
      'Links are limited': 'We link only to titles with a page on this site.',
    }}
    note="The same count is what powers the neighbour list on each title page."
  />
</WikiTip>
